{
	"Name": "Okta - Admin & Configuration Changes - Okta OAuth Client Secret or Credential Accessed or Created",
	"Description": "Alert: Alert - Okta - Admin & Configuration Changes\nMITRE ATT&CK: Credential Access / T1552\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Okta OAuth Client Secret or Credential Accessed or Created\" or \"<ip>|Okta OAuth Client Secret or Credential Accessed or Created\"\n\nOAuth client credential activity: an admin viewing a client secret (app.oauth2.client.read_client_secret, Medium), creating or activating client credentials (app.oauth2.credentials.lifecycle.create / activate, High), or granting an OAuth client admin privileges (app.oauth2.client.privilege.grant, High). Client secrets and keys give API access without MFA; viewing or minting them is a common persistence step.\n\nFalse positives: integration setup by the IAM team.",
